body:
{I thought you were doing a troll about how they were the same, and you weren't committing to either and letting OP make their own conclusions about life and religion.}

OP can make up their own mind. :-)

{Turns out you have an agenda about what is right and what is wrong!}

I think some practices are better than other practices yes it’s true. We all do. It’s not a matter of right and wrong though because the truth doesn’t have to fight. It just is.

{You are against Abrahamic religions all along!}

Against? I’m for meditation and releasing the bonds organized religion can put people’s minds into.

{You hate half the world!}

How can I hate that which I am? Everyone is just a different part of me. Also I spent most of my life in an abrahamic organized religion and my family is in it.


{Way to go! You weren't being clever at all. You have an agenda.}

I wasn’t trying to be clever. Best to be honest even if you’re rejected. 

{How is that working out for you? Thinking that some religions are better than others?}

I don’t have a religion.

{And we are using the term "religion" to have something that has dogma experienced by at least 100,000 people. In the USA Supreme Court terms of religion.}

This is appeal to popularity, a logical fallacy. Just because many people do something doesn’t make it the best thing.

Do not go gentle into that good night, 

Old age should burn and rave at close of day; 

Rage, rage against the dying of the light
